{% load site_tags %}
{% comment %}
"Opening: <show>" — the mailing that goes out for a show opening.

Modelled on the Mailchimp announcements this replaced, in the same order, because that shape was
already working and readers recognise it:

  Opening: <name>          an invitation sentence, naming the curator
  📅 🕓 📍                  the three facts somebody needs to turn up, on their own lines
  hero image
  the show's own description
  whatever the curator wrote for this mailing
  a button to the show
  a few works

Everything comes from the Show row and its Events, so nobody retypes a date and nobody sends a
reception time that changed last week. Reused for every show: pick the template, pick the show.
The masthead, the "Come visit" block, the address and the unsubscribe link come from the shell in
templates/email/campaign_base.mjml.

Available in context (gallery/campaigns.py::show_context):
  show, show_url, artworks, events, opening, closing, curators, site
  campaign_body / campaign_body_blocks — the curator's own words for this one, if any

`opening` is the show's first Event, which is the reception in the ordinary case. There is no
field marking one, so a show with no events falls back to its own start date rather than
rendering a hole where the invitation should be.
{% endcomment %}
<mj-section padding="16px 24px 0">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text font-size="28px" font-weight="bold" padding="8px 0 10px">
      {% if show.show_type == 'open_studio' %}Open Studio: {% else %}Opening: {% endif %}{{ show.name }}
    </mj-text>

    {% comment %}
      The invitation, as one sentence. Unbroken in the source so it stays greppable and testable,
      and so no client wraps it somewhere odd.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if curators %}
    <mj-text padding="0 0 10px">Join us for the opening of {{ show.name }}, a new exhibition curated by {% for c in curators %}{{ c.name }}{% if c.instagram %} (<a href="https://www.instagram.com/{{ c.instagram|cut:"@" }}/" style="color:#198754">@{{ c.instagram|cut:"@" }}</a>){% endif %}{% if not forloop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</mj-text>
    {% else %}
    <mj-text padding="0 0 10px">Join us for the opening of {{ show.name }}.</mj-text>
    {% endif %}
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

{% comment %}
  Date, time, place — the three things a reader needs in order to turn up, each on its own line
  with the emoji the old campaigns used. Big enough to read at a glance on a phone, because this
  is the part people screenshot.
{% endcomment %}
<mj-section padding="0 24px 8px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text font-size="18px" line-height="1.7" padding="8px 0">
      📅 {% if opening %}{{ opening.date|date:"l, j F" }}{% else %}{{ show.start|date:"l, j F" }}{% endif %}<br />
      {% if opening %}🕓 {{ opening.time_range }}<br />{% endif %}
      📍 {% if maps_url %}<a href="{{ maps_url }}" style="color:#222222">{{ site_name }}</a>{% else %}{{ site_name }}{% endif %}
    </mj-text>
    {% comment %}
      "Up through", not "until" or "on until": both leave a reader unsure whether the last day is
      included, which is the same ambiguity the closing mailing had in reverse.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if show.start != show.end %}
    <mj-text color="#666666" font-size="14px" padding="0 0 8px">Up through {{ show.end|date:"j F Y" }}.</mj-text>
    {% endif %}
    {% comment %}
      Directly under the date, because that is the moment a reader decides to come. Two links
      rather than one: Google is a URL, and the .ics covers Apple Calendar and Outlook. No
      JavaScript is possible in an email, so links are the whole mechanism.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if opening_calendar %}
    <mj-text font-size="14px" padding="0 0 10px">
      📅 Add to calendar:
      <a href="{{ opening_calendar.google }}" style="color:#198754">Google</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="{{ opening_calendar.ics }}" style="color:#198754">Apple/Outlook</a>
    </mj-text>
    {% endif %}
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

{% if show.image %}
<mj-section padding="8px 24px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-image src="{{ show.image.url }}" alt="{{ show.name }}" padding="0" href="{{ show_url }}" />
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
{% endif %}

{% if show.description %}
<mj-section padding="8px 24px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text padding="8px 0">{{ show.description|text_blocks|linebreaksbr|truncatewords_html:80 }}</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
{% endif %}

{% comment %}
Anything the curator wrote for this particular mailing — a birthday, a last-minute talk, a
sentence about one piece. This is what stops a reusable format meaning identical wording.
{% endcomment %}
{% if campaign.body_markdown.strip %}{{ campaign_body }}{% endif %}

<mj-section padding="0 24px 8px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-button href="{{ show_url }}" background-color="#198754" color="#ffffff" padding="16px 0">
      See the show
    </mj-button>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

{% if artworks %}
{% comment %}
  Three works, one row. More than three and the columns are too narrow to read on a phone, where
  MJML stacks them anyway; Gmail also clips a message over 102KB, which would take the
  unsubscribe link with it.
{% endcomment %}
<mj-section padding="0 24px 16px">
  {% for artwork in artworks|slice:":3" %}
  <mj-column width="33%">
    {% if artwork.card_md %}
    <mj-image src="{{ artwork.card_md.url }}" alt="{{ artwork.name }}" padding="4px" href="{{ show_url }}" />
    {% endif %}
    <mj-text font-size="13px" align="center" padding="4px" line-height="1.4">
      {{ artwork.name }}
      {% if artwork.artists.all %}<br /><span style="color:#888888">{% for a in artwork.artists.all %}{{ a.name }}{% if not forloop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>{% endif %}
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
  {% endfor %}
</mj-section>
{% endif %}

{% if events|length > 1 %}
<mj-section padding="0 24px 16px">
  <mj-column>
    <mj-text font-weight="bold" font-size="14px" padding="8px 0 4px">Also on</mj-text>
    {% for event in events %}{% if not forloop.first %}
    <mj-text font-size="14px" padding="2px 0">
      {{ event.date|date:"j F" }} · {{ event.time_range }} — {{ event.name }}
    </mj-text>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
{% endif %}
